Package: gstudio
License: GPL (>= 2)
Title: Tools Related to the Spatial Analysis of Genetic Marker Data
Type: Package
Authors@R: person(given = c("Rodney", "J."),
    family = "Dyer",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "rjdyer@vcu.edu")
Description: Provides classes and functions for the spatial analysis of
    genetic marker data, including population structure, genetic diversity,
    distance, and relatedness statistics. The S3 'locus' class allows loci
    to be stored in the same data frame as non-genetic data for
    manipulating and querying multilocus genotypes. Standard estimators of
    genetic diversity, genetic distance, and population differentiation are
    implemented, along with the network construction and analysis tools of
    the formerly separate 'popgraph' package, which represent population
    genetic structure as graph-theoretic networks as described in Dyer and
    Nason (2004) <doi:10.1111/j.1365-294X.2004.02177.x> and Dyer (2015)
    <doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-112414-054150>. Methods are included for
    evaluating network asymmetry, for estimating directional gene flow with
    Gaussian kernels and perplexity-tuned Markov flow partitioning, and for
    inferring the direction of gene flow from genetic gravity, along with
    tools for individual-based simulation. Spatial and geographic data are supported through 'sf',
    'ggplot2', and interactive 'leaflet' maps.
URL: https://github.com/dyerlab/gstudio, https://dyerlab.github.io/gstudio/
